S651 Number-Theory Tournament Carriers
======================================

Thesis
------
A tournament fits number theory when a pairwise arithmetic observable is
collapsed to a binary orientation while the side channel that made the
observable meaningful is kept nearby.

Assumption Challenge
--------------------
I did not assume tournament vertices must be primes, runners, or arcs.
Alternate vertex sets considered: residue classes, gaps, local primes,
Dirichlet characters, zero modes, Frobenius classes, Selmer local
conditions, divisor/valuation strata, height packets, circle-method arcs,
and proof obligations.

Preserved predicates: pairwise lead in prime races; local admissibility for
linear prime forms; and route quality under retained side channels.
Destroyed data: exact prime locations, zero ordinates, analytic estimates,
global primality, Selmer arithmetic, height inequalities, and embeddings.

Prime-Race Tournaments
----------------------
Observable: pi(X;q,a)-pi(X;q,b) for reduced residue classes a,b mod q.
Switch/gauge: orient a -> b when pi(X;q,a) > pi(X;q,b); ties go to lower residue.
Tie Hamiltonian path: residue classes sorted by (-count, residue).
Dynamic variant: orient a -> b when a led b at more prime checkpoints up to X.

