Hard-Problem Carrier Atlas
--------------------------
- Riemann_Hypothesis
  raw scalar: all nontrivial zeta zeros on Re(s)=1/2
  hidden witness: cancellation in primes via explicit formula
  retained side channels: zero spectrum, prime races, Mellin/Fourier modes, Euler product
  plausible tournament vertices: residue classes, zeros, Fourier modes, proof obligations
- Generalized_RH_Chebotarev
  raw scalar: zeros / Frobenius equidistribution
  hidden witness: character and conjugacy-class cancellation
  retained side channels: Dirichlet characters, Frobenius classes, Artin L-functions, prime races
  plausible tournament vertices: characters, conjugacy classes, residue classes, zeros
- Twin_Primes
  raw scalar: gap 2 occurs infinitely often
  hidden witness: admissible pair survives local obstructions and parity barrier
  retained side channels: local residues, singular series, sieve weights, level of distribution
  plausible tournament vertices: local primes, residue classes, gaps, sieve weights
- Goldbach
  raw scalar: every large even N has p+q=N
  hidden witness: additive convolution of primes stays positive
  retained side channels: local residues, major arcs, minor arcs, representation counts
  plausible tournament vertices: residue pairs, prime-pair edges, circle arcs, proof obligations
- BSD
  raw scalar: analytic rank equals algebraic rank
  hidden witness: L-function vanishing order matches Mordell-Weil/Selmer data
  retained side channels: Frobenius traces, local root numbers, Selmer groups, regulators, Tamagawa factors
  plausible tournament vertices: primes of good reduction, Frobenius traces, Selmer classes, local conditions
- abc
  raw scalar: height controlled by radical up to epsilon
  hidden witness: valuation-side channel prevents too much additive/multiplicative alignment
  retained side channels: prime valuations, radical, height, conductor/discriminant, Szpiro channel
  plausible tournament vertices: prime divisors, valuation strata, height packets, elliptic curve conductors
- Euler_Heegner_Rabinowitsch
  raw scalar: finite lucky prime horizon
  hidden witness: class-number-one/no-early-collapse side channel
  retained side channels: discriminant, class group, norm factorization, boundary square
  plausible tournament vertices: input slots, boundary positions, class group states, proof obligations
- Collatz
  raw scalar: all orbits reach 1
  hidden witness: 2-adic/3-adic carry defect remains controlled
  retained side channels: parity word, rapidity defect, 2-adic state, 3-adic inverse tree
  plausible tournament vertices: parity states, defect packets, residue classes, proof obligations

