Reading
-------
Prime races are the cleanest literal tournament: residue classes compete,
and edge flips are zero-driven wall crossings.  This is a finite shadow of
GRH/explicit-formula data, not a replacement for it.

Twin primes, Goldbach, Sophie Germain primes, and prime tuples become local
obstruction tournaments only after the local product ledger is retained.
The product says which quotient survives local tests; it does not decide
the global conjecture because parity barriers and minor-arc/global
correlations are destroyed by the quotient.

For RH/BSD/abc, the tournament move is moral progress rather than proof:
choose vertices as zeros, Frobenius traces, local conditions, valuations,
or proof obligations, then ask which quotient preserves the hard predicate.
The route tournament says the strongest transferable first move remains
side-channel jackknife/local ledgers, with raw scalar numerology last.
